Subject: [PATCH 4/31] i8259: withdraw an unacknowledged cascade request

When the slave masks a pending request behind a timer ISR, its INT output
falls but the master retains IRQ2 in IRR. Timer EOI then acknowledges a stale
cascade with no eligible slave request. OPENSTEP's spurious IRQ15 path omits
master EOI and subsequent disk interrupts remain blocked by ISR2.

Withdraw the pending cascade on falling IRQ2 in cascaded mode. Preserve ISR
priority, guest-selected SFNM, and the existing ordinary IRQ pulse contract.
Exclude single-controller mode. Test wired slave masking, normal nesting,
SFNM, AEOI, and input withdrawal/reassertion. The OPENSTEP installer progresses
past its former CD-root stall under TCG without changing guest binaries.

Intel's pre-INTA input requirement motivates withdrawal; this is a focused
cascade correction, not a complete two-cycle INTA timing model. The migration
layout is unchanged. Physical 8259/PIIX measurements remain unavailable.

---
